That’s a very strong principle for the whole Pantheon.

Don’t let every experience modify instinct equally.

The better supported the consequence, the more permission it has to alter the road network.

For example:

w=
\begin{cases}
1.0 & \text{EXECUTED + externally verified}\\
0.7 & \text{OBSERVED}\\
0.4 & \text{strongly INFERRED}\\
0.1 & \text{SPECULATIVE}\\
0 & \text{IMAGINED only}
\end{cases}

Then route learning becomes:

\Delta G
=
\eta
\cdot
\text{outcome}
\cdot
\boxed{\text{evidential weight}}

rather than blindly:

\Delta G=\eta\cdot\text{whatever felt successful}.

That’s the old PNIS inside the new PNIS.

The ancestor becomes an organ.

